# PB Exchange — Frontend (Vite) Environment
#
# Copy to ".env" and adjust. Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the
# browser bundle, and they are INLINED AT BUILD TIME (`npm run build`), not read at
# runtime — changing this file requires a rebuild. Never put secrets here: anything
# in this file ends up readable in the shipped JS.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_URL — full base URL of the backend API (including /api/v1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fallback when unset: "/api/v1" (see apps/web/src/api/client.ts)
#
# LOCAL DEV  -> leave unset/commented. The Vite dev server proxy in vite.config.ts
#               already forwards "/api" to http://localhost:4000.
#
# IIS        -> leave unset. The site's web.config reverse-proxies "/api/*" to
#               localhost:4000, so the relative path works.
#
# SPLIT DEPLOY (frontend and backend on different domains, e.g. two Render
#               services) -> set it to the backend's full URL:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api/v1
